{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Withers, etc.</b> After it is like grass, it withers; and after it is like a flower, it fades. Only the word of HaShem endures — as in, stands firm — and there is none who can turn it back." "<b>For the spirit of YHWH.</b> The meaning: the spirit that He sends blows upon the grass and it withers."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:05.279435068Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}